      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 4.95,
          "en": "So now that you have an idea of what Angular is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.95,
          "end": 7.38,
          "en": "and why you might wanna use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.38,
          "end": 11.19,
          "en": "before we start writing Angular code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 14.19,
          "en": "there's one important thing you need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.19,
          "end": 18.66,
          "en": "and understand about Angular the framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.66,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "It is a framework that keeps on evolving",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 26.04,
          "en": "and innovating, though it does that in a very stable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.04,
          "end": 29.22,
          "en": "and backward-compatible way, which is also important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.22,
          "end": 32.85,
          "en": "because, of course, you don't wanna relearn Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 34.23,
          "en": "every year or so.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.23,
          "end": 37.53,
          "en": "But it's worth noting that Angular 2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.53,
          "end": 42.3,
          "en": "the first version of Angular was released back in 2016,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.74,
          "end": 47.49,
          "en": "and it was Angular 2 and not Angular 1",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.49,
          "end": 50.46,
          "en": "because Angular one is technically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 52.26,
          "en": "a totally different framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.26,
          "end": 56.4,
          "en": "which is now called AngularJS, which was created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.4,
          "end": 57.66,
          "en": "by the same team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 60.33,
          "en": "or at least some team members were the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.33,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "But Angular 2 was a total rewrite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 64.68,
          "en": "a totally different framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.68,
          "end": 68.19,
          "en": "But since then, there have been new versions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.19,
          "end": 71.25,
          "en": "of Angular coming out every year,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.25,
          "end": 75.48,
          "en": "or actually two new major versions every year",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.48,
          "end": 80.31,
          "en": "because the Angular team adopted a release policy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.31,
          "end": 83.25,
          "en": "or strategy where they try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.25,
          "end": 87.75,
          "en": "to release a new major version every six months.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.75,
          "end": 91.89,
          "en": "But, and that's really important, this does not mean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 95.4,
          "en": "that Angular changes every six months",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.4,
          "end": 100.4,
          "en": "and that what you learned is obsolete after six months.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.56,
          "end": 102.12,
          "en": "The opposite is the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.12,
          "end": 106.71000000000001,
          "en": "Angular has been a super stable framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.71000000000001,
          "end": 110.46000000000001,
          "en": "and if you were to learn Angular 2 today,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.46000000000001,
          "end": 113.85,
          "en": "most of the code you'd write would still work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.85,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "with the latest Angular version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 119.28,
          "en": "because whilst the Angular team has indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.28,
          "end": 121.26,
          "en": "changed some things over time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.26,
          "end": 124.02,
          "en": "and has added some new features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 128.58,
          "en": "it always did that in a very backward-compatible way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.58,
          "end": 133.17,
          "en": "so that what you learned back then is still relevant today.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.17,
          "end": 136.47,
          "en": "Of course, with this course, I wanna teach Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.47,
          "end": 140.01,
          "en": "to everyone who wants to work with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 144.75,
          "en": "But the truth is that since we have all these versions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 147.84,
          "en": "not all teams and companies use",
